course: dictionary
lesson: 16103
title: Webbed: feet and webs
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Webbed means having skin joining the toes or fingers together. «Ducks have webbed feet, so they can paddle across the pond.» The clue is paddle: webbed feet push water, like little paddles.
explain: Webbed can also mean covered with or made like a web. «The old shed was webbed with cobwebs.» The clue is cobwebs: the walls were covered with spider threads.
explain: Ask what the sentence is about. If it is about swimming, animals or feet, webbed means joined by skin. If it is about threads or spiders, it means covered with a web. Then swap your meaning into the sentence to check it makes sense.
fact: Webbed feet have skin joining the toes together.
fact: Ducks, geese, swans, penguins, frogs, platypuses and otters all have webbed feet.
fact: Webbed feet work like paddles, pushing more water when an animal swims.
fact: «Webbed» can also mean covered with or made like a web, as in «webbed with cobwebs».
fact: Some people are born with slightly webbed toes, which is usually harmless.
exercise: Which animal has webbed feet to help it swim? | *A duck | A horse | A cat | A rabbit
exercise: «Ducks have webbed feet, so they can paddle across the pond.» What does webbed mean here? | Made of wood | Very wet and muddy | Covered with cobwebs | *Having skin joining the toes
exercise: «The corner of the garden shed was webbed with dust and threads.» What does webbed mean here? | *Covered with or made like a web | Very clean and shiny | Painted bright red | Joined together by skin
test: Why do webbed feet help ducks swim? | They stop the ducks getting wet | They keep the feet warm | *They work like paddles, pushing more water | They make the feet smaller
test: Which phrase best explains «webbed toes»? | Toes that are painted | Toes that can grip branches | Toes that are very long | *Toes joined together by skin
exam: «The frog kicked its webbed feet and shot across the pond.» What helped the frog move so quickly? | Its short tail | The sun | *Its webbed feet | The wind
